sequenceDiagram
  %% Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review (2026-11-06): the Gateway holds each Route-serving Node from admission to the terminal state; a second Route write on it waits (docs/reference/routes.md#coordinate-publication).
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task + full intent as inputs, R1-R4, single-swamp-node; DECISIONS scope (SQLite only when chosen, Schedules move, cert from destination CSR in-run), 1 (signing is the one step→Gateway call), DNS hold retired (PR #2443); tightened by flow-tighten 2026-11-02 (rules 3, 6, 8, 13); .env and Processes as in instance.create. docs/reference/instance-transfer.md.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 5, 17, 22 (destination preflight from recorded state; cfgmgmt file/systemd, Route publish as in route:create).
  %% Decided: Nick 2026-11-02, .env.testing only for an owned MySQL/PostgreSQL database, written by the same file step.
  %% status: draft
  %% Interim: the run signs inside the Route child, and SQLite copies stay refused. The Swamp steps below are the real workflow steps.
  %% command: instance:transfer
  %% kind: instance.transfer
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane S icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane D icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant S as Node 12<br/>source · over ssh
  participant D as Node 15<br/>destination · ssh
  CLI->>GW: instance:transfer 42 15
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:transfer 42 15`
  %%> - syntax: `<instance> <node> [--name=NAME] [--sqlite-source-path=PATH] [--force] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - moves development Instance 42 from Node 12 to Node 15; the Instance id and Project stay
  %%> Confirmation:
  %%> - without `--force`, the CLI asks for consent that names the source, destination and downtime; the default is No
  %%> - without a terminal, or with `--json`, `--force` is required
  %%> Options:
  %%> - `--name`: another Instance name on Node 15
  %%> - `--sqlite-source-path`: currently refused with `operation.kind_unavailable`; no database file moves
  Note over CLI: Confirm the downtime
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - asks for default-No consent naming the source, destination and old-placement deletion
  opt --name
    Note over GW: Set destination name
    %%> What it changes:
    %%> - uses the supplied name for the destination path and generated domain instead of keeping the Instance name
  end
  opt --sqlite-source-path
    GW--xCLI: SQLite copy unavailable<br/>operation.kind_unavailable
    %%> Result:
    %%> - refuses before reservation or any run; the steps below do not run
  end
  Note over GW: Preflight, render .env<br/>Instance 42 · task #5133
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has access grants to Node 12 and Node 15
  %%> - both Nodes have the `app-dev` role and belong to active Clusters
  %%> - Project 7 may be placed on Node 15, and the destination path and planned ports are free, from Node 15's recorded Instances and Processes
  %%> - Instance 42 is an active development Instance with one active Route, and no removal runs
  %%> Plans:
  %%> - the Processes from Project 7's definitions for `development`, with Node 15's ports
  %%> - the Route on Node 15, and the Schedules' new target
  %%> Renders .env:
  %%> - from the stored environment of Instance 42, with Node 15 values such as `APP_URL`
  %%> - `.env.testing` only when Instance 42 owns a database on a MySQL or PostgreSQL server: `.env` with `APP_ENV=testing` and the test database credentials
  %%> Result:
  %%> - Instance 42 marked transferring; task #5133 recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Pause Schedule triggers<br/>workflow trigger removal
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - removes the native Swamp schedule trigger of each Schedule of Instance 42
  %%> - there is no Node work here; Schedules install nothing on Nodes
  %%> Why:
  %%> - no fire runs against Node 12 during the move
  GW->>SW: Push .env to the vault<br/>vault: env-5133
  %%> Why:
  %%> - `.env` can hold secrets, which travel only through the vault
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the run reads it with `vault.get`; no step asks the Gateway for it
  Note over GW: Hold the Route Nodes
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - holds each Node that serves this Route's site (Caddy and PHP) from admission to the terminal state
  %%> - a second Route write on one of those Nodes waits (task status `waiting`) and starts when the Node is free, oldest first
  %%> Not held:
  %%> - the DNS Node: its records are keyed, and the apply phase refuses a file that changed since the read
  %%> Limit:
  %%> - two Route writes on one Node run one after the other, so each waits for the other's whole run
  %%> - a newer write waits behind an older waiting one that shares a Node, and a waiting write can be cancelled
  %%> - a timed-out write keeps its Nodes until Swamp confirms that its run stopped, or for 15 minutes
  %%> - task provision and cancel, instance:register and the Cluster Router writes hold the Nodes for their Route-publish step only, through the `route-hold` call
  %%> - a task that waits starts from the Node's live files; a site block that matches none of its captured states still stops it with `owned_revision_conflict`
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-transfer
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one run of `operation-instance-transfer` on Swamp serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - both Nodes' addresses and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> - paths, Process plan, Route plan, SQLite path when chosen
  %%> - secrets only as vault key names
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5133
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>S: Stop source Processes<br/>process child · forEach
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - stops the Processes of Instance 42 on Node 12; downtime starts here
  %%> Keeps:
  %%> - the Process units, for a restore if the move fails
  SW->>S: Archive the checkout<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · tar
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the Git directories, then packs the Git history, branch, origin, index, unstaged edits and untracked files
  %%> - refuses a shared common repository or alternates (`instance.transfer_source_shared`, `instance.transfer_source_invalid`)
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - `.env`; the Gateway renders a new one for Node 15
  SW->>S: Copy the archive to 209<br/>@swamp/ssh copy · from
  SW->>D: Copy it to the destination<br/>@swamp/ssh copy · to
  %%> How:
  %%> - through private scratch space on 209; archive bytes never enter results
  SW->>D: Unpack the checkout<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · tar
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - extracts into the destination path, refusing an existing path (`instance.transfer_destination_exists`)
  SW->>D: Make it standalone<br/>git config core.bare
  SW->>D: Drop the worktree config<br/>git config --unset-all
  %%> Why:
  %%> - a linked worktree becomes an independent checkout on Node 15
  SW->>D: Create the orbit-env group<br/>cfgmgmt/group apply
  SW->>D: Write .env<br/>cfgmgmt/file · 0640 orbit-env
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the `.env` the Gateway rendered from Instance 42's stored configuration for Node 15, from `vault.get`, as root: owned by the Node user with group `orbit-env`, mode 0640
  %%> Requires:
  %%> - stored configuration; admission refuses an Instance without it (`env.configuration_missing`)
  SW->>D: Run Project setup steps<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · in order
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - runs the Project's setup steps as in `instance:create`, so dependencies match Node 15; the first failure restores the source
  SW->>D: Prepare Route workloads<br/>route workload child
  SW->>D: Create, start Processes<br/>process child · forEach
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - creates the Instance's Processes on Node 15 and starts them; stopped ones stay stopped
  SW->>D: Publish the Route<br/>route-mutation-forward
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - signs the CSR through the Gateway primitive, installs the certificate and site on Node 15, and reloads Caddy
  %%> Cutover:
  %%> - a ready result makes Node 15 authoritative
  SW->>D: Check the destination<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · curl
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one `curl` with the Route's domain as SNI: the site answers; a Project without a Route skips it
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the end check before the source is retired; a failure keeps the source for repair
  alt destination published
    SW->>S: Remove source Processes<br/>process child · forEach
    Note over SW: Prepare source retirement
    %%> Why:
    %%> - hand the source path, SSH pins and host-only source Node checkout inventory to the shared removal phase
    SW->>S: Retire the source<br/>Ansible · tags remove
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the shared destroy guard checks live Git dependencies immediately before removal; a late worktree keeps the source intact
    %%> - removes a linked worktree through Git, with no rm fallback on refusal or unregister failure
    %%> If it fails:
    %%> - Node 15 stays authoritative; retain the domain refusal and dependent paths/IDs before cleanup; mark the task failed
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader reads the run's steps and the Route child's ready result
    Note over GW: Record Node 15<br/>Instance, Processes, Route
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Instance 42, its Processes and its Routes are recorded on Node 15, in one change
  else a step fails before cutover
    SW->>S: Restore the Route<br/>route-mutation-restore
    SW->>S: Restore the source<br/>process child · forEach
    SW->>D: Remove new Processes<br/>process child · forEach
    SW->>D: Discard the destination<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · rm -rf
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes the unpacked checkout, and only after the restore succeeded
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    Note over GW: Keep Node 12, mark failed<br/>rerun is safe
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Instance 42 stays on Node 12; a run that only restored also fails (`instance.transfer_failed`)
  end
  Note over SW: Clean retirement files
  %%> When:
  %%> - after preparation and retirement settle, also on failure
  SW->>S: Remove the source archive<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · rm
  SW->>D: Remove the copied archive<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · rm
  Note over SW: Remove the 209 archive<br/>rm · always
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5133
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
